message: >
  If you use MATH-SYNC, please cite this software release using
  the Zenodo DOI and the metadata in this file.

type: software

title: >
  MATH-SYNC v1.0: Reproducible Computational Pipeline for Robust
  and Identifiable Affine-Clock Alignment of Heterogeneous
  Multirate Sensor Streams

version: "1.0"

date-released: "2026-09-23"

authors:
  - family-names: "Hechavarria-Hernandez"
    given-names: "Jesus Rafael"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9013-8665"
    affiliation: "Universidad ECOTEC"

license: MIT

repository-code: "https://github.com/jrhechavarriah/MATH_SYNC_v1.0"

keywords:
  - clock synchronization
  - temporal alignment
  - affine clock model
  - clock skew
  - robust estimation
  - Huber M-estimation
  - identifiability
  - multirate sensor streams
  - multimodal sensing
  - reproducibility

abstract: >
  MATH-SYNC v1.0 is a reproducible computational pipeline for robust
  and identifiable affine-clock alignment of heterogeneous multirate
  sensor streams. The release includes controlled synthetic validation,
  semi-synthetic perturbation-and-replay using public Harvard timing
  schedules, within-participant session replication, participant-level
  Harvard replication, external schedule-replay replication using WESAD,
  participant-level inference, manuscript-aligned tables and figures,
  supplementary sensitivity analyses, automated tests, and SHA-256
  integrity manifests.

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22920440"

